WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.682 --> 00:00:02.001
- I have a plan.

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:03.078
- You've got a plan?

00:00:03.078 --> 00:00:05.345
- I have part of a plan.

00:00:05.345 --> 00:00:06.899
I actually had to get rescued

00:00:06.899 --> 00:00:08.482
one time by the girl I was dating.

00:00:08.482 --> 00:00:09.315
- [Seth Meyers] Oh no.

00:00:09.315 --> 00:00:10.148
- Yeah.

00:00:10.148 --> 00:00:12.649
My brother and I both were
going to be a stuntman team

00:00:12.649 --> 00:00:15.465
and we would throw each other
down the stairs to practice.

00:00:15.465 --> 00:00:16.420
I'd walk around and be like,

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:18.114
"Hi, I'm from Meineke, here you go.

00:00:18.114 --> 00:00:19.537
"Four oil changes, $20.

00:00:19.537 --> 00:00:20.788
"Pretty great, right?

00:00:20.788 --> 00:00:21.966
"Cash, check or credit card today

00:00:21.966 --> 00:00:23.499
"and we'll take that, no?

00:00:23.499 --> 00:00:25.732
"Okay, (laughing) you too sir."

00:00:25.732 --> 00:00:29.497
- He's an American actor and
one of my personal favorites.

00:00:29.497 --> 00:00:32.112
He achieved leading man
status after staring in

00:00:32.112 --> 00:00:34.376
The Lego Movie and
Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:00:34.376 --> 00:00:36.805
In 2015, he was named by Time Magazine,

00:00:36.805 --> 00:00:41.258
one of the top 100 Most
Influential People in the World.

00:00:41.258 --> 00:00:43.296
- Alright, so I'm just going
to meditate for 20 minutes

00:00:43.296 --> 00:00:44.431
and then we'll get this going.

00:00:44.431 --> 00:00:46.464
(laughing)

00:00:46.464 --> 00:00:48.418
- He's Chris Pratt and he is our take

00:00:48.418 --> 00:00:50.482
on his Top 10 Rules for Success.

00:00:50.482 --> 00:00:52.289
Rule number two is our personal favorite,

00:00:52.289 --> 00:00:54.787
and we would love to know
what hit a home run for you.

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:56.989
And, make sure to stick
around 'til the end

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:59.877
to hear my special message to Chris Pratt.

00:00:59.877 --> 00:01:02.588
(flying sound)

00:01:02.588 --> 00:01:05.505
(intriguing music)

00:01:12.963 --> 00:01:13.986
- I have a plan.

00:01:13.986 --> 00:01:15.287
- You've got a plan?

00:01:15.287 --> 00:01:17.617
- I have a part of a plan.

00:01:17.617 --> 00:01:19.357
- What percentage of a plan?

00:01:19.357 --> 00:01:20.751
- I don't know, 12 percent.

00:01:20.751 --> 00:01:24.124
- 12 percent? (laughing)

00:01:24.124 --> 00:01:25.159
- That's a fake laugh.

00:01:25.159 --> 00:01:26.550
- It's real.

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:27.383
- Totally fake.

00:01:27.383 --> 00:01:30.483
- That is the most real,
authentic, hysterical laugh

00:01:30.483 --> 00:01:33.153
of my entire life because
that is not a plan.

00:01:33.153 --> 00:01:33.986
- I am Groot.

00:01:33.986 --> 00:01:35.949
- So what if it's better than 11 percent.

00:01:35.949 --> 00:01:37.450
What the hell does that
have to do with anything?

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.283
- Thank you.

00:01:38.283 --> 00:01:41.950
Groot's the only one
of you that has a clue.

00:01:43.568 --> 00:01:44.459
- Ugh.

00:01:44.459 --> 00:01:47.164
- You come to Hollywood and
you're chasing this dream

00:01:47.164 --> 00:01:49.641
you want to be an actor, you know?

00:01:49.641 --> 00:01:53.471
There's not a ton of milestones
that are crystal clear

00:01:53.471 --> 00:01:55.270
that you know what they look like.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:57.149
Because, for the most part,

00:01:57.149 --> 00:02:00.724
the things that are going to
help you get to your goal,

00:02:00.724 --> 00:02:03.595
are movies that haven't been written yet.

00:02:03.595 --> 00:02:06.057
They're jobs that haven't existed yet.

00:02:06.057 --> 00:02:09.228
You're kind of giving
yourself over to this thing,

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:12.581
saying like, please, I don't
want to be a waiter anymore,

00:02:12.581 --> 00:02:14.206
I want to be an actor, you know?

00:02:14.206 --> 00:02:15.039
- [Male] Yeah.

00:02:15.039 --> 00:02:17.863
- And, so there's very few
things that are crystal clear.

00:02:17.863 --> 00:02:20.364
Like, images of what you would want.

00:02:20.364 --> 00:02:24.575
But, one of them is to work with an icon.

00:02:24.575 --> 00:02:26.101
To work with somebody
like a Steven Spielberg,

00:02:26.101 --> 00:02:29.434
and so that, to me, was one of my goals.

00:02:30.275 --> 00:02:31.647
You wouldn't even want to say it out loud

00:02:31.647 --> 00:02:32.840
'cause it'd be so ridiculous.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:33.673
- [Male] Right, yeah.

00:02:33.673 --> 00:02:34.666
- What do you want to do kid?

00:02:34.666 --> 00:02:36.445
Well, I want to work
with Steven Spielberg.

00:02:36.445 --> 00:02:38.045
And, they'd be like, "Uh, I don't know."

00:02:38.045 --> 00:02:39.337
(laughing)

00:02:39.337 --> 00:02:41.931
Some jobs you learn by going to college

00:02:41.931 --> 00:02:44.013
and they give you an education

00:02:44.013 --> 00:02:45.524
and then you'd bring that to your work.

00:02:45.524 --> 00:02:48.706
And, some jobs you learn
by just being on the job.

00:02:48.706 --> 00:02:51.275
And, from Cursed Part 3 on,

00:02:51.275 --> 00:02:53.309
all the way up to Jurassic World,

00:02:53.309 --> 00:02:55.401
my knowledge of how to be on a set,

00:02:55.401 --> 00:02:58.984
how to act, and how to
handle myself on set

00:02:59.903 --> 00:03:02.349
and approach work is continuing to grow.

00:03:02.349 --> 00:03:03.642
I've learned a lot on every job.

00:03:03.642 --> 00:03:06.648
It would be smart, when
on a job, to be a sponge.

00:03:06.648 --> 00:03:08.073
Pick somebody and learn from them.

00:03:08.073 --> 00:03:08.906
I'm getting to the point now

00:03:08.906 --> 00:03:11.100
where I have more experience than a lot

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.206
of the people that are on the set

00:03:12.206 --> 00:03:13.524
and I'm actually at the point where

00:03:13.524 --> 00:03:15.773
I can teach other people,
so that's pretty cool too.

00:03:15.773 --> 00:03:18.298
- So, another thing is,
well, you're riding horses.

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:19.450
- Yeah, I'm riding a ton of horses.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:21.523
- Is this a skill you had
previous to this film?

00:03:21.523 --> 00:03:22.669
- Oh, gosh, no.

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:23.669
I have been,

00:03:25.425 --> 00:03:26.679
I'm bad, bad.

00:03:26.679 --> 00:03:29.260
I guess that's how I would
describe my horse riding skill.

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:30.146
- Would the horses agree?

00:03:30.146 --> 00:03:31.521
Do you think they could sense your--

00:03:31.521 --> 00:03:32.354
- Most definitely.

00:03:32.354 --> 00:03:33.187
- Okay.

00:03:33.187 --> 00:03:34.730
- Yep, those horses, they can sense it.

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:36.113
And they see me, and I'm a big guy

00:03:36.113 --> 00:03:38.130
and they're like, alright buddy,

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:41.099
don't get on me and not know how to ride.

00:03:41.099 --> 00:03:42.926
You're too heavy to carry around

00:03:42.926 --> 00:03:44.228
if you don't know how to ride.

00:03:44.228 --> 00:03:45.894
And, I get on there and
I'm like, "Howdy cowboy."

00:03:45.894 --> 00:03:48.230
And they're like, ah, (bleep)

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:49.063
(laughing)

00:03:49.063 --> 00:03:50.161
But, I get, you know--

00:03:50.161 --> 00:03:50.994
- So, in your whole career,

00:03:50.994 --> 00:03:52.366
you've never had to ride
a horse for anything?

00:03:52.366 --> 00:03:53.736
- Never for any kind of movies, no.

00:03:53.736 --> 00:03:56.398
I was embarrassed on horses
a few times in my life,

00:03:56.398 --> 00:03:58.930
growing up, so I had a
contentious relationship with--

00:03:58.930 --> 00:03:59.763
- [Seth] Okay.

00:03:59.763 --> 00:04:00.596
- The equain.

00:04:00.596 --> 00:04:01.810
- And, was it just that you lacked

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:03.945
the fundamental understanding
of how horses were?

00:04:03.945 --> 00:04:05.539
- I treated them like jet skis.

00:04:05.539 --> 00:04:06.372
- Okay, gotcha.

00:04:06.372 --> 00:04:07.205
(laughing)

00:04:07.205 --> 00:04:08.038
- I was like, I know, I'm
just going to jump on you

00:04:08.038 --> 00:04:09.614
and hit the gas and you go, right?

00:04:09.614 --> 00:04:10.447
- [Seth] Gotcha.

00:04:10.447 --> 00:04:11.280
- And, they're like, I'm a living being,

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:12.113
I'm going to crush you now.

00:04:12.113 --> 00:04:12.946
- [Seth] Okay, gotcha.

00:04:12.946 --> 00:04:14.551
- I just didn't, I
didn't fully put together

00:04:14.551 --> 00:04:16.705
that it was a living animal,

00:04:16.705 --> 00:04:18.696
a breathing being.
- Well, why would you?

00:04:18.696 --> 00:04:19.529
- Why would you?

00:04:19.529 --> 00:04:20.727
Who gives a (bleep)?

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:21.560
(laughing)

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:22.400
No, but I would just jump and say,

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:27.096
and also, my confidence would
quickly outgrow my skill.

00:04:27.096 --> 00:04:28.979
Like, in almost everything in my life.

00:04:28.979 --> 00:04:29.812
- Okay.

00:04:29.812 --> 00:04:30.645
(laughing)

00:04:30.645 --> 00:04:31.611
So, you only need to do something

00:04:31.611 --> 00:04:32.565
for a second to think I got it.

00:04:32.565 --> 00:04:33.565
- To think I got this.

00:04:33.565 --> 00:04:34.398
- Right.

00:04:34.398 --> 00:04:35.231
- Yeah.

00:04:35.231 --> 00:04:36.636
Oh, so you hit with this and it walks?

00:04:36.636 --> 00:04:38.270
Going to hit it real
hard and make it sprint.

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:39.359
- [Seth] Okay.

00:04:39.359 --> 00:04:40.482
- And then, yeah, I actually had

00:04:40.482 --> 00:04:43.154
to get rescued one time
by the girl I was dating.

00:04:43.154 --> 00:04:43.987
- [Seth] Oh no.

00:04:43.987 --> 00:04:44.820
- Yeah.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.466
- The both of you were on horses?

00:04:46.466 --> 00:04:48.722
- We were on horses,
we were on this beach,

00:04:48.722 --> 00:04:49.555
it was supposed to

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:50.734
be romantic.
- So romantic, yeah.

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:53.517
- And then, the horse
just took off running

00:04:53.517 --> 00:04:55.825
and my feet came out of the stirrups.

00:04:55.825 --> 00:04:57.336
And, my feet were up in the air

00:04:57.336 --> 00:05:00.173
and I was holding the
very end of the reins.

00:05:00.173 --> 00:05:01.006
(laughing)

00:05:01.006 --> 00:05:05.250
And, my head was bouncing off
of the back of horses ass.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:06.715
I was seconds from death.

00:05:06.715 --> 00:05:08.625
This thing is going about 40 miles an hour

00:05:08.625 --> 00:05:11.315
down a rocky beach, I was like,
this is it, I'm going to die.

00:05:11.315 --> 00:05:14.263
And, I hear, (whistle) yah, yah.

00:05:14.263 --> 00:05:16.430
And, then the girl just,

00:05:17.442 --> 00:05:19.848
just totally rides up and saves the day.

00:05:19.848 --> 00:05:22.791
She had to grab my reins
and calm the horse.

00:05:22.791 --> 00:05:24.390
"Yah, yah."

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.329
And, I was just like,
that was it after that.

00:05:26.329 --> 00:05:28.541
And, that moment, we broke up in my head.

00:05:28.541 --> 00:05:29.388
(laughing)

00:05:29.388 --> 00:05:30.221
- Yeah.

00:05:30.221 --> 00:05:31.459
(multiple speakers)

00:05:31.459 --> 00:05:32.292
- In her head too.

00:05:32.292 --> 00:05:34.109
She was like, yeah, I used to like you

00:05:34.109 --> 00:05:35.491
but this is over,
- This probably ended it.

00:05:35.491 --> 00:05:36.324
- Yeah.

00:05:36.324 --> 00:05:37.392
- You are a stuntman at heart.

00:05:37.392 --> 00:05:39.240
- Yeah, that's what I
wanted to be when I grew up,

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:41.012
when I was a kid, I
wanted to be a stuntman.

00:05:41.012 --> 00:05:44.223
And, my brother and I, both,
were going to be a stuntman team

00:05:44.223 --> 00:05:47.668
and we would throw each other
down the stairs to practice.

00:05:47.668 --> 00:05:50.655
Never get injured, we would
just like fall out of trees

00:05:50.655 --> 00:05:52.593
and hit each other with the car,

00:05:52.593 --> 00:05:54.535
or fall off a bike, or
do like cool stunts.

00:05:54.535 --> 00:05:58.577
And so, the fact that I
get to do some stunts,

00:05:58.577 --> 00:06:00.183
I shouldn't say that I do all my stunts,

00:06:00.183 --> 00:06:02.772
I have Joe Bucaro, who
is an excellent stuntman.

00:06:02.772 --> 00:06:04.409
And, we have a great stunt crew

00:06:04.409 --> 00:06:06.328
that works really hard on our show,

00:06:06.328 --> 00:06:08.157
but when they write something physical

00:06:08.157 --> 00:06:09.489
and like a physical comedy bit,

00:06:09.489 --> 00:06:12.015
I'll usually try one
or two on my own to do,

00:06:12.015 --> 00:06:13.085
and that's really fun.

00:06:13.085 --> 00:06:14.528
What I think is so cool about
the Guardians of the Galaxy

00:06:14.528 --> 00:06:16.859
is it opens up the universe.

00:06:16.859 --> 00:06:19.952
So, instead of taking these new things

00:06:19.952 --> 00:06:22.533
and bringing them right back
to the stories we already know,

00:06:22.533 --> 00:06:24.387
I think it's like, open it up,

00:06:24.387 --> 00:06:26.860
see what other corners of
the galaxy we can discover.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:29.351
Bring in characters
that weren't, you know,

00:06:29.351 --> 00:06:31.309
bring in characters that were from some

00:06:31.309 --> 00:06:32.610
of the Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:34.349
Like, explore Yondu, explore the origins

00:06:34.349 --> 00:06:35.473
more of these characters.

00:06:35.473 --> 00:06:37.774
And, if it is Thanos, explore
the Infinity Gauntlet.

00:06:37.774 --> 00:06:39.408
Like, how many of these
stones is he going to get?

00:06:39.408 --> 00:06:41.907
And, who does that open up?

00:06:41.907 --> 00:06:43.642
The universe expands, you know?

00:06:43.642 --> 00:06:45.239
And, looking out on it, we
want to take these characters

00:06:45.239 --> 00:06:46.548
and bring them into the Avengers

00:06:46.548 --> 00:06:48.774
and we want to have them be
all in the same movie together.

00:06:48.774 --> 00:06:50.701
It's like, no, that,
make a hundred movies,

00:06:50.701 --> 00:06:51.981
you know what I mean?

00:06:51.981 --> 00:06:52.814
- Yeah.

00:06:52.814 --> 00:06:53.647
(laughing)

00:06:53.647 --> 00:06:55.435
- And, if they end up
crossing over, great.

00:06:55.435 --> 00:06:57.038
I lived in Maui, yeah.

00:06:57.038 --> 00:06:59.073
- And, but you didn't live in a fancy way?

00:06:59.073 --> 00:07:01.003
- (Laughing) Yeah.

00:07:01.003 --> 00:07:04.414
I lived in a van in Maui for
about a year, when I was 19.

00:07:04.414 --> 00:07:05.247
- [Ellen] Yeah.

00:07:05.247 --> 00:07:06.080
- Yeah, and so--

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:07.191
- That van, right there.

00:07:07.191 --> 00:07:08.114
(laughing)

00:07:08.114 --> 00:07:08.947
- Is that the van?

00:07:08.947 --> 00:07:09.780
Wow.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:10.613
- Would that be you and the van?

00:07:10.613 --> 00:07:12.786
- That's me and that's
literally the script

00:07:12.786 --> 00:07:15.573
that got me out of Maui.

00:07:15.573 --> 00:07:17.165
That script is for Cursed Part 3,

00:07:17.165 --> 00:07:19.441
the movie that I got paid $700 to do that.

00:07:19.441 --> 00:07:20.449
- $700?

00:07:20.449 --> 00:07:21.282
- I know!

00:07:21.282 --> 00:07:22.287
I was like, score!

00:07:22.287 --> 00:07:23.395
(laughing)

00:07:23.395 --> 00:07:25.448
I lived in a van, I was like, yeah!

00:07:25.448 --> 00:07:26.646
(applause)

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:27.479
To act?

00:07:27.479 --> 00:07:28.312
Okay.

00:07:28.312 --> 00:07:29.145
Woo, hoo!

00:07:30.569 --> 00:07:32.571
That $700 lasted me one year.

00:07:32.571 --> 00:07:34.235
- I bet if they didn't know
you you lived in a van,

00:07:34.235 --> 00:07:35.244
you would've gotten more money.

00:07:35.244 --> 00:07:36.858
But, it's like, anything will,

00:07:36.858 --> 00:07:39.510
we can give him $400, he'll take it.

00:07:39.510 --> 00:07:40.343
(laughing)

00:07:40.343 --> 00:07:43.522
So, then you went back to shoot
this movie, Jurassic World.

00:07:43.522 --> 00:07:46.102
How cool is that to go
back and shoot a giant,

00:07:46.102 --> 00:07:48.735
big blockbuster when you
lived in a van there?

00:07:48.735 --> 00:07:52.153
- It's so surreal in one of those weird,

00:07:52.153 --> 00:07:54.696
full-circle things that happens in life.

00:07:54.696 --> 00:07:56.899
Like, when I was there, I mean,

00:07:56.899 --> 00:07:58.528
I was having the time of my life,

00:07:58.528 --> 00:08:00.293
you know, at 19 years old,

00:08:00.293 --> 00:08:04.505
just like, living in a
car with my friend and--

00:08:04.505 --> 00:08:06.562
- So, oh, there was another
guy in there with you?

00:08:06.562 --> 00:08:07.668
- Yeah, I had a roommate, yeah.

00:08:07.668 --> 00:08:08.501
- Oh.

00:08:08.501 --> 00:08:09.334
(laughing)

00:08:09.334 --> 00:08:10.167
- Yeah, I had a roommate.

00:08:10.167 --> 00:08:11.737
Yeah, it wasn't lonely,
it was pretty awesome.

00:08:11.737 --> 00:08:12.877
There was two of us.
- Uh, yeah. (laughing)

00:08:12.877 --> 00:08:14.077
- [Female In Audience] What attracted you

00:08:14.077 --> 00:08:16.933
to the character of Star-Lord?

00:08:16.933 --> 00:08:19.092
- You know, for me, what
I got really excited about

00:08:19.092 --> 00:08:20.781
was that, this is an earthling.

00:08:20.781 --> 00:08:23.719
This is a kid who was nine years old,

00:08:23.719 --> 00:08:25.552
just like me, in 1988.

00:08:27.029 --> 00:08:29.670
I was nine years old and so was he.

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:30.859
(laughing)

00:08:30.859 --> 00:08:35.026
So, you got to think, this
is a kid who saw Star Wars.

00:08:35.958 --> 00:08:38.264
This is a kid who saw Indiana Jones

00:08:38.264 --> 00:08:41.029
and saw Back to the Future.

00:08:41.029 --> 00:08:42.358
And Footloose.

00:08:42.358 --> 00:08:46.158
And all the movies that
I loved when I was a kid.

00:08:46.158 --> 00:08:49.749
So, if he gets, if it
were me and I was him

00:08:49.749 --> 00:08:51.635
and something tragic happened

00:08:51.635 --> 00:08:54.561
and then immediately after,
I was transported to space

00:08:54.561 --> 00:08:55.954
and essentially given a spaceship

00:08:55.954 --> 00:08:59.579
and an opportunity to become
whoever the hell I wanted to be

